<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Michael (the Highwaymen)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1960</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement, No. 1 in 1961</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Michaël (Rika Zaraï)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1964</span><span class="sg-chain-h">French version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Michael, bring dein Boot an Land (Ronny)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">German version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Hört, wen Jesus glücklich preist</span><span class="sg-chain-h">German gospel version (a song of the Beatitudes)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A Man Named King (Greg &amp; Steve)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1989</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same tune, new words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Glory Be to God on High</span><span class="sg-chain-h">hymn to Saletan's melody</span></li></ul></section>
